1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,950
An AI agent that manages my to-do list. LEFT: Todoist (the to-do list). RIGHT: the AI agent (where I type).

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,450
A to-do list that an AI can edit
LEFT: Todoist, a to-do app with 5 tasks.  RIGHT: the code running the AI agent; I chat with it in the box at the bottom.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:19,250
Request 1: I type a plain-English sentence
“Hi! Can you please add make tomato sauce to my to-do list?”

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,950
Done: “make tomato sauce” appears in the list
The agent replied “I’ve added…” and updated the real to-do list. No clicking in Todoist.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,950
Request 2: same idea, a new task
“Can you please add fix car”

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,950
Done: “fix car” is added
Two new tasks so far, both created just by typing.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,450
Request 3: now I ask it to remove a task
“Awesome! Now can you please remove buy an apple? I went to the grocery store yesterday.”  Even with the extra chatter, it works out which task I mean.

8
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,950
Done: “buy an apple” is gone
The agent found the right task in the list and removed it.

9
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:51,950
Request 4: one more, phrased casually
“What about buy bananas? I got those there too!”  I never say “remove” this time, and the agent still gets it.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:03,950
Done: “buy bananas” is gone too
4 typed sentences = 4 real changes.  Final list: get a new tire, buy icecream, buy a new camera, make tomato sauce, fix car.

11
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:20,350
The AI is handed 3 tools to choose from
The highlighted line of code lists them: add_task, show_tasks, remove_task. For each sentence I type, the AI picks the tool that fits.

12
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,195
AI that takes action, not just answers
Plain English in, real changes out.

13
00:01:22,245 --> 00:01:27,145
4 requests in plain English. 4 real changes in Todoist.
